# Documentation Rules

Keep documentation lightweight and useful for rapid AI-assisted development.
Prefer links to canonical material over repeating the same requirement in multiple files.

## Canonical locations

- Product/technical scope → `docs/core-scope/`
- Visual/design work → `docs/DesignConcept/`
- Implementation tickets → `docs/devTickets/phase{N}/`
- Upcoming queue → `docs/devTickets/devTickets_next.md`
- Completion registry → `docs/devTickets/devCompletion.md`

## Core-scope responsibilities

- `01-Project-Overview.md` — identity/purpose.
- `02-Core-Scope.md` — current product boundaries.
- `03-User-Flows.md` — user journeys and behaviour.
- `04-Screens-and-UX.md` — screens and functional UX.
- `05-Data-Model.md` — canonical data.
- `06-Calculation-Rules.md` — canonical derived-domain/calculation behaviour.
- `07-API-Specification.md` — API design intent.
- `08-Future-Scope.md` — deferred/non-current scope.

Do not duplicate these specifications into tickets or Cursor rules.

## Design documentation

Do not preload `docs/DesignConcept/`. Start from `docs/DesignConcept/README.md` or `00_UI-Design-Concept.md`.

- `00_UI-Design-Concept.md` is the visual-language source of truth (palette, motion, authority).
- Component `.visual.md` files are the signature-widget source of truth.
- `core-visual-component-requirements.md` is an inventory, not a second spec.
- `ui-component-architecture.md` is file placement / layering only.
- `react-ui-library-strategy.md` is for library choice only.
- Canonical names: `GoalJourneyTrack`, `DailyTargetGauge`, `WeeklyAccountabilityRibbon`.
- `GoalStateCompanion/` and `ReferenceItems/` are not MVP reading unless the ticket says so.
- Figma layout is not binding; tokens live in `00_UI-Design-Concept.md`.
- Visual conflict: DesignConcept wins. Status/calculation conflict: core-scope / `06` wins.
- If design and core functional scope still disagree after that, flag it rather than silently choosing.

## Dev ticket format

Tickets should be concise and include:
- Status, Phase, Depends On
- Related Docs / Design References
- Objective and user outcome
- Scope and explicit Out of Scope
- Likely Files/Areas
- Technical Tasks
- Acceptance Criteria
- Verification
- Completion Notes when implemented

Tickets reference canonical docs rather than reproducing long visual or calculation specifications.
When completed, mark criteria, set status to Implemented, and update queue/completion registries.

## Alignment

If code, ticket, API spec, calculations, or design docs drift materially, record and resolve the
mismatch in the relevant ticket/doc instead of leaving silent divergence.

Do not create unsolicited documentation dumps, speculative architecture docs, or future-scope tickets.
